From 1d829457f00ea63bf6543c136ce58ca285ada831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:43:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] Verify send outcomes through the local L1 pair and Base
 node receipt source

Composes worker E's FINAL source-binding adapters (createL1PairSource,
createBaseNodeSource; work/rpc-transaction-independence c08331e9) into the
independent consumers. network/tx-evidence/ holds them byte for byte
(PROVENANCE.json: sha256 and git blob of each file); they are never edited here.

network/receipt-source.mjs builds both adapters from one config file
(enclave-receipt-source/v1, loopback only), fixes the accepted trust
('local-validated-pair'; 'test-fixture' identities only inside a test harness,
ENCLAVE_TEST_RECEIPT_FIXTURE=1), accepts evidence only through E's
acceptEvidence (minted, kind, trust), and binds a minted receipt to the intended
transaction: its hash is keccak256 of the signed bytes (held, or the transport's
transaction object re-encoded with its own signature), the sender is recovered
from that signature and must be the receipt's `from` and the intended sender, and
the nonce comes from those bytes. It is not a verifier; inclusion, status and
level come only from the minted receipt.

Consumers (--receipt-source FILE, with --chain-verifier):
- VerifiedChain.verifyOutcome / sendQuorumTx: with a source, the transport's
  receipt is not consulted; the source is polled for THIS hash; the state
  verifier must reach the inclusion block and show the nonce consumed (two local
  authorities that disagree decide nothing). A revert is final only on a minted
  receipt that says so. Not-ready, foreign-L1 or tampering sources end UNKNOWN.
- external signer: resolve/attach/wallet-send/rebroadcast confirm, revert or
  mismatch only on a minted receipt for a transaction bound to the intent's
  sender and nonce; a consumed nonce or post-state alone is not inclusion. The
  transport's nonce search only names a candidate. Journals persist facts, never
  the minted object (shownEvidence).
- credit-vault CLI: reconcile's executing transaction is bound and its inclusion
  and status minted; mint/submit/relay sends verified.
- enclave CLI: --receipt-source FILE; `receipt-source status` prints both
  adapters' readiness checks verbatim. Trust and level are shown as minted.
Without --receipt-source every path keeps its explicit-transport labels.

Tests: test/receipt-source.test.mjs (anvil + E's labelled fixtures) and
test/receipt-source.e2e.test.mjs (reth --dev Base execution + Helios + anvil L1 +
E's labelled beacon/rollup fixtures: every receipt is trust 'test-fixture').
